# Third-party notices

RAI is licensed under Apache-2.0 (see `LICENSE`). This file is the attribution
that travels with it.

The `rai` binary is statically linked: every crate listed below is compiled
into the executable in the release archives, so its license terms apply to
those bytes. Reproduced here are the full texts, grouped by license, with the
crates each one covers.

**Do not edit this file by hand.** It is generated from the dependency graph of
`classeve-rai-infer` with its default `cli` feature — the crate and feature set
the release archives are built from — by:

```
cargo about generate --manifest-path rai-infer/Cargo.toml \
    -c about.toml about.hbs -o THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
```

CI regenerates it and fails if the committed copy has drifted, so a dependency
bump cannot quietly change what is being distributed without changing what is
being attributed.

The memory-service crates (`rai-server`, `rai-core`, `rem-nra`) are excluded:
they are not part of RAI and appear in no release archive.

